    {
      "id": "q-4",
      "type": "mcq",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "prompt": "Residuals are +3 and -3. Why not average them as the error score?",
      "options": [
        "Averages cannot handle negative values",
        "The model is perfectly correct",
        "Squaring would make them cancel",
        "Their average is zero despite two wrong predictions"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "explanation": "The signed mean hides errors. MSE is (9+9)/2=9."
    },
    {
      "id": "q-5",
      "type": "mcq",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "prompt": "What unit does rent MSE have?",
      "options": [
        "BDT squared",
        "BDT",
        "Square metres",
        "No unit under every definition"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explanation": "The residual is measured in BDT, so its square has BDT squared units."
    },
    {
      "id": "q-6",
      "type": "mcq",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "prompt": "If both slope and intercept move, what replaces a one-dimensional cost curve?",
      "options": [
        "A list of target labels",
        "A two-parameter cost surface",
        "A mandatory straight cost line",
        "A single unchanged number"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "explanation": "There are two adjustable coordinates and a cost height for each pair."
    },
    {
      "id": "q-7",
      "type": "mcq",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "prompt": "Does the lowest training MSE guarantee the best future predictions?",
      "options": [
        "Yes, even after repeated test tuning",
        "Yes, if the model has enough powers",
        "No; model choice still needs held-out evaluation",
        "Only when MSE is printed to three decimals"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "explanation": "Optimisation and generalisation answer different questions."
    },
    {
      "id": "q-8",
      "type": "output",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "prompt": "What MSE comes from residuals 1,-1,2,-2?",
      "options": [
        "0.0",
        "10.0",
        "1.5",
        "2.5"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "explanation": "The squares sum to 10; divide by four to get 2.5.",
      "code": "errors = [1, -1, 2, -2]\nprint(f\"{sum(e*e for e in errors)/len(errors):.1f}\")\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "q-9",
      "type": "output",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "prompt": "What does sklearn report for predictions [3,3] against targets [2,4]?",
      "options": [
        "1.0",
        "0.0",
        "2.0",
        "4.0"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explanation": "Both gaps have magnitude one, so MSE is one.",
      "code": "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\nprint(f\"{mean_squared_error([2,4],[3,3]):.1f}\")\n",
      "requires": [
        "sklearn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q-10",
      "type": "output",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "prompt": "If every residual doubles, by what factor does MSE change?",
      "options": [
        "2",
        "4",
        "1",
        "8"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "explanation": "Squaring a doubled gap multiplies its contribution by four.",
      "code": "a = [1, 2]\nb = [2*v for v in a]\nprint(sum(v*v for v in b)//sum(v*v for v in a))\n"
    }
  ],
  "keyPoints": [
    {
      "en": "Signed residuals can cancel while predictions remain wrong.",
      "bn": "অনুমান ভুল হলেও ধনাত্মক আর ঋণাত্মক ফাঁক কাটাকাটি হতে পারে।"
    },
    {
      "en": "MSE averages squared gaps and cannot be negative.",
      "bn": "MSE ফাঁকের বর্গের গড়; এটা ঋণাত্মক হয় না।"
    },
    {
      "en": "The cost curve is conditional on any fixed intercept.",
      "bn": "intercept আটকে রাখলে cost-এর রেখাটাও সেই শর্ত মেনে চলে।"
    },
    {
      "en": "Both slope and intercept can affect the loss.",
      "bn": "ঢাল আর intercept দুটোই ভুলের পরিমাণ বদলাতে পারে।"
    },
    {
      "en": "Large errors receive a strong squared penalty.",
      "bn": "বড় ভুলের বর্গ বেশি বাড়ে, তাই MSE-তে তার প্রভাব বেশি।"
    }
  ],
  "examQuestions": [
    {
      "type": "numerical",
      "question": "Compute MSE of slope 1 and intercept 1.4 on the five market observations.",
      "marks": 5,
      "answerHtml": "<p>Predictions are 2.4,3.4,4.4,5.4,6.4. Residuals are 0.6,0.6,0.6,-1.4,2.6. Squares sum to 0.36+0.36+0.36+1.96+6.76=9.8. MSE=9.8/5=1.96.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "numerical",
      "question": "Residuals are +3,-3. Compare signed mean and MSE.",
      "marks": 5,
      "answerHtml": "<p>The signed mean is zero, which hides both mistakes. Squared residuals are 9,9, so MSE=18/2=9 target units squared.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "long",
      "question": "Explain why the fixed-intercept cost minimum need not be the full best line.",
      "marks": 8,
      "answerHtml": "<p>A slope chart is a one-dimensional slice of a two-parameter surface. Restricting b can prevent reaching the full optimum. A sampled grid can also miss the exact continuous minimum even within that slice.</p>"
    }
